TEXT 160 0 Left 3 ;#10 Simple amplifier, seen DC coupled and AC coupled
TEXT 160 64 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hkq-fvb5-NI
TEXT 160 112 Left 2 ;The collector carries a 1 kHz signal sitting on a DC level. Cscope and Rscope are a scope
TEXT 160 144 Left 2 ;input switched to AC coupling: a capacitor in series with the input resistance.
TEXT 1430 256 Left 2 !.tran 0 1 990m 1u
TEXT 1430 296 Left 2 !.meas tran VC_AVG AVG V(collector) FROM 995m TO 1
TEXT 1430 336 Left 2 !.meas tran VC_PP PP V(collector) FROM 995m TO 1
TEXT 1430 376 Left 2 !.meas tran VB_PP PP V(base) FROM 995m TO 1
TEXT 1430 416 Left 2 !.meas tran VE_AVG AVG V(emitter) FROM 995m TO 1
TEXT 1430 456 Left 2 !.meas tran VAC_AVG AVG V(scope_ac) FROM 995m TO 1
TEXT 1430 496 Left 2 !.meas tran VAC_PP PP V(scope_ac) FROM 995m TO 1
TEXT 1430 536 Left 2 !.meas tran GAIN PARAM VC_PP/VB_PP
TEXT 160 816 Left 2 ;Alan's drawing gives 20k, 10k, 2k and 390 ohm and marks the supply only as VCC. The 12 V rail
TEXT 160 848 Left 2 ;and the 1.87 V offset, 0.2 V, 1 kHz drive are chosen here to hold the collector near mid rail.
TEXT 160 896 Left 2 ;He feeds the input straight onto the divider node, so the source sets the base DC level and the
TEXT 160 928 Left 2 ;divider only loads it. His title reads GAIN =~ -2.5, while -Rc/(Re+re) here comes out near -5.
TEXT 160 976 Left 2 ;A scope couples through about 1 uF; 100 nF settles inside this run and still passes 1 kHz unchanged.
